From: Motion Browser Fork Maintainers <motion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Feb 2025 10:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0002] motion: package — fork manifest package fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Purpose
=======
Give Motion builds the fork applicationId `com.motion.browser.chromium`.

The PREFERRED mechanism is the build arg (already present in the canonical
template motion/gn/args.gn, see docs/BUILD_CHROMIUM.md §6):

    chrome_public_manifest_package = "com.motion.browser.chromium"

This patch documents that path inside the build file and provides a fallback
default so a plain Motion build without a hand-written args.gn still lands on
the fork package. The declare_args() guard means the value is only filled
when the global arg is unset.

Rebase notes
============
- The applicationId override path in GN is `chrome_public_manifest_package`
  (consumed by the chrome_public_apk manifest packaging step). If upstream
  renames or re-homes this arg, port the arg name here and in args.gn —
  never drop the Motion package identity.
- Insertion point is the top of chrome/android/BUILD.gn, right after the
  license header; a drift in surrounding imports is expected and harmless
  (apply_patches.sh tolerates offset context).

Honesty note (spec §77)
=======================
Authored against the upstream file layout as documented for 130.0.6723.58.
NOT verified against a real Chromium checkout — rebase expected.
---
 chrome/android/BUILD.gn | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/android/BUILD.gn b/chrome/android/BUILD.gn
index 2b7c8d9e..0f1e2d3c 100644
--- a/chrome/android/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/android/BUILD.gn
@@ -1,5 +1,17 @@
 # Copyright 2014 The Chromium Authors
 # Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 # found in the LICENSE file.
 
+# Motion (0002): fork package identity.
+# Preferred mechanism: set the same arg in args.gn (see motion/gn/args.gn):
+#   chrome_public_manifest_package = "com.motion.browser.chromium"
+# This block only fills the value when the global arg is unset, so plain
+# Motion builds get the fork applicationId without extra configuration.
+declare_args() {
+  motion_use_fork_package = true
+}
+if (motion_use_fork_package && !defined(chrome_public_manifest_package)) {
+  chrome_public_manifest_package = "com.motion.browser.chromium"
+}
+
 import("//build/config/android/config.gni")
